The '''First Battle Memorial'''<ref name="Episode Guide">{{SW|url=explore/the-clone-wars/ep518|text="The Jedi Who Knew Too Much" - ''The Clone Wars'' Episode Guide|nolive=1}}</ref> was a commemorative monument in honor to the many [[clone trooper]]s who [[Death|died]] during the first [[First Battle of Geonosis|battle]] of the [[Clone Wars]] on [[Geonosis]]. The monument was constructed on an enormous slab of [[Geonosian]] rock, and the wall was engraved with the designations of the fallen [[Cloning|clones]]. It was located on the outside plaza of the [[Imperial Inspectorate HQ|Republic Center for Military Operations]] on [[Coruscant]].<ref name="Much Trivia">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/the-jedi-who-knew-too-much-trivia-gallery|text="The Jedi Who Knew Too Much" Trivia Gallery|quote=The monument at the center of the Republic military base plaza is an enormous slab of Geonosian rock that lists the names of the clone troopers that fell in action in the first battle of the Clone Wars.}} {{C|Slide 9}}</ref>

In [[19 BBY]],<ref name="Solitary Date">{{Disney|subdomain=press|domain=co.uk|url=press-kit/star-wars:-the-bad-batch-season-2|text=Star Wars: The Bad Batch, Season 2 Press Kit}} places [[The Bad Batch Season 2|''The Bad Batch'' Season 2]] [[Standard month|months]] after [[The Bad Batch Season 1|''The Bad Batch'' Season 1]], which can be placed in and around [[19 BBY]] per ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''. Therefore Season 2 takes place in approximately the same [[Standard year|year]].</ref> [[Vice Admiral]] [[Edmon Rampart|Rampart]] ordered [[Elite Squad Trooper]] [[Crosshair|CT-9904]] "Crosshair" to report to the memorial at 0900 [[Standard hour|hours]]. [[Gender|He]] reunited with [[Clone Commander]] [[Cody|CC-2224]] "Cody" before they departed for the [[mission to Desix]].<ref name="The Solitary Clone" />

==Behind the scenes==
The [[Aurebesh]] "headline" inscription in the middle of the monument is mirror-inverted and says "BATTLT TT [[Geonosis|GEONOSIS]]," and some of the Ts are sideways or upside-down.<ref name="Knew Too Much" /> According to the Trivia Gallery for "[[The Jedi Who Knew Too Much]]" on [[StarWars.com]], it is supposed to read "BATTLE OF GEONOSIS," and the rest of the memorial is supposed to list the designations of the [[clone trooper]]s that [[Death|fell]] during the [[First Battle of Geonosis]];<ref name="Much Trivia" /> the latter is also stated in the Trivia Gallery for "[[The Solitary Clone]]."<ref name="Solitary Trivia">{{SW|url=the-solitary-clone-trivia-gallery|text="The Solitary Clone" Trivia Gallery &#124; The Bad Batch|quote=The monument behind Crosshair and Cody during their first discussion is the First Battle Memorial, a huge slab of Geonosian rock engraved with designations of the fallen troopers from the first battle of the Clone Wars.}} {{C|Slide 3}}</ref> However, when translated, the rest of the Aurebesh inscriptions turn out to be nothing but meaningless gibberish.<ref name="Knew Too Much" /><ref name="The Solitary Clone" />
